// Phase 11 Plan 5 (NAT-06, PLAN.md Task 2): a two-hop forwarding
// ("relay") chain for the four-tier interprocedural differential.
//
// The NATURAL relay shape -- a SINGLE declared borrow (`-> borrow(buffer)
// Buffer`) carried across BOTH hops, forwarded leaf-to-relay-to-main
// exactly like testdata/phase08/relay_depth2_refuse.lang's own middle
// hop -- was attempted first and found UNAVAILABLE at this maturity, for
// the reason testdata/phase10/relay_depth3_accept.lang's own header
// documents in full: `corevalidate.peerDeriveOriginFacts` has no
// `core.OpCall` case, so a function whose declared borrow return is
// SOURCED FROM FORWARDING A CALL'S RESULT is unconditionally judged
// "not derived" and refused as not-`Callable`, independently of whatever
// `check` decides -- and that same header confirms this affects
// `relay_depth2_refuse.lang`-shaped programs too, not only depth-3 ones.
// This is D-10-C01 / PHASE-11-DEBT.md's own carried-forward Phase 10 gap,
// restated here because this fixture is the first Phase 11 corpus member
// to actually need the shape it constrains.
//
// NEAREST EXPRESSIBLE SHAPE (this fixture, generalizing
// relay_depth3_accept.lang's own technique down to depth 2): `relay`
// creates a genuine LOCAL borrow of its own parameter, forwards that
// borrow into a real call to `leaf` (exercising the call boundary with a
// borrowed value), and -- once that borrow's last use is the `leaf` call
// -- takes ownership of its own parameter and returns it OWNED, not
// borrowed. The overall call chain still reaches the declared two-hop
// shape (`main` -> `relay` -> `leaf`, two real `core.OpCall` operations),
// and a genuine borrow is created, forwarded across ONE call boundary,
// and released -- but the loan itself crosses only that one hop, never
// all the way back to `main`, because a two-hop DECLARED-ORIGIN carry is
// exactly the shape the gap above makes unrepresentable as an accepting
// program today.

module phase11.multi_function_relay_depth2

export {
  fn main
}

fn leaf(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let observed = borrow buffer
  observed
}

fn relay(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let observed = leaf(borrowed)
  let taken = take buffer
  taken
}

fn main(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let result = relay(buffer)
  result
}
